IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-p1-other`

-- Tests for ucta-p1-other.l4 (sections 8 to 10; section 8 is blank in this text).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `s 9(1) - effect of termination on reasonableness`

-- The term has to satisfy the requirement and the contract has been terminated: it may be found to do so.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract term may be found to satisfy the requirement of reasonableness and be given effect` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The contract is still in force: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract term may be found to satisfy the requirement of reasonableness and be given effect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The term need not satisfy the requirement: the "Where" fails (ruling of 2026-11-05, a failed "where" on a positive grant is the text's no).
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract term may be found to satisfy the requirement of reasonableness and be given effect` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the contract term may be found to satisfy the requirement of reasonableness and be given effect` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 9(2) - affirmation`

-- "this does not of itself exclude the requirement of reasonableness".
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract of itself excludes the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract of itself excludes the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract of itself excludes the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 10 - evasion by means of secondary contract`

-- All three limbs: "A person is not bound by any contract term ...".
#ASSERT `s 10 the person is bound by the contract term` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- This Part does not prevent the other from excluding the liability (the "so far as" limit): the section says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 10 the person is bound by the contract term` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Whether this Part prevents it is not known.
#ASSERT `s 10 the person is bound by the contract term` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The rights do not extend to the enforcement of another's liability.
#ASSERT `s 10 the person is bound by the contract term` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The term does not prejudice rights under another contract.
#ASSERT `s 10 the person is bound by the contract term` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Item 2 of the fix round: s 9(2) in its own words`

-- "Where on a breach the contract is nevertheless affirmed by a party entitled to treat it as repudiated, this does not of itself exclude the requirement of reasonableness in relation to any contract term".
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract does not of itself exclude the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "Where" is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): affirmed without a breach, or a breach without affirmation.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract does not of itself exclude the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract does not of itself exclude the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) affirming the contract does not of itself exclude the requirement of reasonableness in relation to the contract term` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
